From 953e4b728ae34c29ab74eac5c40dc5a349311682 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:01:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] licences: the S-X8 UNRESOLVED item is CLOSED - the author's
 own LICENSE and NOTICE are retained

Phase 1 left one item UNRESOLVED: MarlaLabs' own licence file had never been fetched, so the retention was the canonical Apache-2.0 text with no copyright line. Both of the author's files are now retained verbatim, with source URL, fetch date and sha256 recorded in NOTICE and in licenses/README.md.

S-X8-MarlaLabs-LICENSE.txt: 11350 bytes, sha256 ad4aa936adb43842a3f34d16797acdd39ba4f523e5b02b9ea4fe48b1962d3c74, carrying the line a stand-in could not supply - 'Copyright 2026 Marti Vidal Leandro'. S-X8-MarlaLabs-NOTICE.txt: 1278 bytes, sha256 20ea964a519ef0b04ce51beb2ae0cf601a82775cd7e4022c15ec0434a94ca13a. Retaining the NOTICE is not optional: Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires it to travel, and it also carries the base model's attribution (Qwen3.8-27B, Qwen Team / Alibaba Group, Apache-2.0), which now travels with this tree too.

Independently confirmed at the DOI: the Zenodo record for 10.5281/zenodo.21922640 carries "license": {"id": "apache2.0"} in its own metadata and names Vidal Leandro, Marti (MarlaLabs) as rights holder.

licenses/Apache-2.0.txt, the licensor-neutral stand-in added earlier the same day, is REMOVED: the author's own file does that job and two copies of the same terms invite the reader to wonder which governs. The author's NOTICE is deliberately EXCLUDED from the path/identity scrub - it contains his contact address, and a NOTICE that Apache-2.0 requires to travel verbatim is not ours to edit.

Fetched with crwl and aria2c per tool law. Everything on the fetched pages was treated as data; no instruction found there was followed.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - licence and notice files only; no code path is touched.
